From 3ea5d417424d55c981c3fa8f1b01a1f4bab07b59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaoyi Chen <chaoyi.chen@rock-chips.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:33:46 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: Fix the extra iommu_group_get call in
 rocket_job_handle_irq

The rocket attaches the IOMMU group in rocket_job_run() and detaches it
in rocket_job_handle_irq(). Calling  iommu_group_get() in
rocket_job_handle_irq() causes the reference count to increase
unexpectedly. And this causes rocket_core_fini() to fail to release the
IOMMU group, leading to a resource leak.

[jh: carried unchanged from Chaoyi Chen's posting of 2026-08-14, which is
 still unapplied. The Fixes tag is corrected: rocket_job_handle_irq() and
 the line this patch changes were both added by 0810d5ad88a1, and
 658ebeac3351 does not touch rocket_job.c at all. ZhaoJinming sent the
 same one-line change earlier, on 2026-06-09, bundled with runtime PM
 guards for the IRQ handler, and that series stalled on the second half.]

Fixes: 0810d5ad88a1 ("accel/rocket: Add job submission IOCTL")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260814022453.437-4-kernel@airkyi.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260610071045.3414828-2-zhaojinming@uniontech.com/
Signed-off-by: Chaoyi Chen <chaoyi.chen@rock-chips.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index f40435505..1b4c0f38f 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@ static void rocket_job_handle_irq(struct rocket_core *core)
 				return;
 			}
 
-			iommu_detach_group(NULL, iommu_group_get(core->dev));
+			iommu_detach_group(NULL, core->iommu_group);
 			dma_fence_signal(core->in_flight_job->done_fence);
 			pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(core->dev);
 			core->in_flight_job = NULL;
-- 
